## Notebook vs. Production Code

### When to Use Notebooks (`vitastress_draft.ipynb`)
- Exploratory data analysis (EDA)
- Visualizations and distributions
- Prototyping feature extraction logic
- Quick hypothesis testing
- Generating figures for reports

### When to Use Production Code (`src/`)
- Final feature extraction pipeline
- Model training and evaluation
- Reproducible experiments (RQ1, RQ2, RQ3)
- Batch processing of all subjects
- Hyperparameter tuning
- Cross-validation loops

### Transition Strategy
1. Prototype in notebook → verify correctness with visualizations
2. Refactor into modular functions in `src/`
3. Add comprehensive docstrings and type hints
4. Add unit tests if time permits
5. Use `src/` modules for all final experiments

