## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

### 🚫 Data Leakage
- Never normalize across all data before splitting
- Never use test subject data in any way during training
- Ensure windows don't span across train/test boundaries
- Don't use future labels to inform feature extraction

### 🚫 Temporal Errors
- Don't forget to shift labels forward for prediction horizon
- Verify timestamp alignment across modalities (use `pd.merge_asof`)
- Check for clock drift or timestamp mismatches

### 🚫 Missing Data Assumptions
- Don't assume zeros are valid measurements for physiological signals
- Don't impute missing data without documenting the strategy
- Don't ignore quality flags in activity data

### 🚫 Performance Metrics
- Don't rely solely on accuracy (data is imbalanced!)
- Don't report AUROC without PR-AUC
- Don't forget to report false alarm rates (critical for user trust)

### 🚫 Code Quality
- Don't copy-paste code (refactor into functions)
- Don't leave magic numbers unexplained (use named constants)
- Don't skip docstrings ("I'll add them later" = never happens)
- Don't commit without testing on at least 2 subjects

